Ticket 0001: geocoder_client.geocode() only handled >= 500, so a 404
(unknown venue) crashed on response.json() and surfaced as an unhandled
500. Resolution recorded here and in app/README.md: a 404 is "no result"
(the client returns (None, None), the meetup is still created with 201),
mirroring how a real Nominatim answers an unknown place with 200 [].

app/contracts/geocoder/examples.json gets one new example ("Unknown Venue,
Nowhere" -> 404); the fake needs no change, it already 404s on unlisted
queries. test_meetups.py posts that venue through the real endpoint and
asserts 201 with venue_lat/venue_lon both null.

